.TH std::expected::operatorbool,std::expected::has_value 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::expected::operatorbool,std::expected::has_value \- std::expected::operatorbool,std::expected::has_value

.SH Synopsis
constexpr explicit operator bool() const noexcept; \fB(1)\fP (since C++23)
constexpr bool has_value() const noexcept;         \fB(2)\fP (since C++23)

Checks whether *this represents an expected value.

.SH Return value

has_val

.SH Notes

A std::expected object is never valueless. If has_value() returns true, operator*() can be
used to access the expected value; otherwise, error() can be used to access the unexpected
value.

